research_content:
{
  "research_status": "COMPLETE",
  "research_findings": [
    {
      "topic": "Audience & market context (young professionals using cafés for remote work)",
      "summary": [
        "There is broad evidence that remote work grew in the 2020s and many remote workers use third places (cafés, coworking) for variety and atmosphere, but I did not find a single, nationally representative source that quantifies the exact share of 22–35 year‑olds who regularly work from cafés (2020–2026).",
        "Commonly cited motivations in surveys and qualitative research: better change of scenery, social/ambient stimulation, available Wi‑Fi, and convenient food/drink. Quantitative percentages by the exact 22–35 cohort and by city are not reliably established in public national datasets."
      ],
      "recommended_action": "Avoid asserting a specific percent of 22–35-year-olds work from cafés. If a numeric claim is required, run a short local survey/intercept or use first‑party customer data and report sample and dates."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Instagram Reels platform guidance",
      "summary": [
        "Preferred creative format for Reels is vertical 9:16 (1080 × 1920 px).",
        "15 seconds is an acceptable length for Reels and can perform well for a single, focused message; keep critical copy out of UI-covered ‘unsafe’ edges and test in Instagram/Ads Manager preview.",
        "Best practices: hook in first 1–2 seconds, readable captions / burned‑in text for sound‑off viewers, clear single CTA; use caption field for supplementary details (hours, link prompting directions)."
      ],
      "recommended_action": "Produce a 9:16 master, place the visual/CTA centrally (safe area), burn readable captions for the VO, and preview in Instagram/Ads Manager. Consider an A/B test: 15s vs 22–30s if you want to show more context."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Music & SFX licensing for Instagram Reels",
      "summary": [
        "Instagram’s in‑app music availability and permitted uses depend on account type, territory, and whether the Reel will be promoted/boosted. Business accounts often face restrictions compared with personal accounts.",
        "Meta provides the Meta Sound Collection and guidance for businesses; using in‑app music does not guarantee commercial clearance for boosted/promoted content—some tracks are restricted for commercial use.",
        "A lo‑fi acoustic loop must be cleared for commercial use (organic post vs. paid ad differ); keep written license evidence when using third‑party tracks."
      ],
      "recommended_action": "Use tracks from Meta Sound Collection or obtain a written commercial license that explicitly covers Instagram Reels and paid promotion in your territory. Verify before boosting the Reel."
    },
    {
      "topic": "‘Free fast Wi‑Fi’ — what to mean and how to verify",
      "summary": [
        "There is no single industry standard definition of “fast.” Performance needs depend on number of simultaneous users and activities (browsing vs. HD video calls).",
        "Practical recommended target for cafés: aim for at least ~25 Mbps download and 5 Mbps upload available per typical active user at peak times as a conservative baseline to comfortably support browsing, video calls and screen sharing when contention exists (this is a practical recommendation rather than a legal standard).",
        "Verification should be done with repeated speed tests from multiple customer seats during peak and off‑peak times (use Speedtest and repeat tests; record times/dates/seats). Also consider latency and packet loss for real‑time apps."
      ],
      "recommended_action": "Only use 'free fast Wi‑Fi' if repeat peak‑period, on‑site tests support it. Keep dated test logs (location/seat/time), and if performance varies, refine the claim (e.g., 'free Wi‑Fi suitable for browsing & video calls') or remove the claim."
    },
    {
      "topic": "‘Handcrafted coffee’ and truth‑in‑advertising",
      "summary": [
        "The term 'handcrafted' is not per se illegal in U.S. advertising, but it creates factual expectations about how the product is prepared. Under FTC truth‑in‑advertising standards, the claim must be truthful and not misleading.",
        "If parts of the coffee‑making process are automated or pre‑prepared, the advertiser should be ready to substantiate or to qualify the claim to avoid an impression that conflicts with reality."
      ],
      "recommended_action": "Document what 'handcrafted' means at Brew Haven (who prepares the drink, which steps are manual). If needed, use more specific, verifiable language in creative (e.g., 'pulled to order,' 'latte art by baristas')."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Competitor / creative landscape (café creatives positioning for remote work)",
      "summary": [
        "Public creative patterns that appear effective: show an actual work setup (laptop, outlets, seating), highlight one concrete benefit (Wi‑Fi, outlets, quiet nook), and end with a local CTA.",
        "I could not find three public case studies (2020–2026) that both show a café Reel and provide verified foot‑traffic outcomes; engagement metrics (views/likes) are common but are not proof of visits."
      ],
      "recommended_action": "Collect a small competitive benchmark from local cafés (save Reels, dates, visible messaging) and measure local actions (direction clicks, 'how did you hear' responses) rather than impressions alone."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Practical production constraints & optimizations",
      "summary": [
        "Auto‑captions are available but not perfectly reliable—proof and edit them. Burned‑in captions improve clarity for sound‑off users.",
        "Cover thumbnail matters for profile grid and discovery; choose a frame that clearly communicates the place/benefit.",
        "Text overlay readability and placement: keep it out of the top/bottom UI areas and use large, high‑contrast type for safety on small screens."
      ],
      "recommended_action": "Export a master, create a burned‑in caption track, choose a clear cover frame, preview in the app, and test two opening hooks to compare retention."
    }
  ],
  "verified_claims": [
    "Instagram Reels is optimized for vertical 9:16 (1080 × 1920) creative and previews can cover interface areas — keep critical text in safe zone.",
    "A 15‑second Reel is an acceptable length for a single straightforward message on Instagram Reels.",
    "Meta/Instagram music availability and permitted uses differ by account type, territory, and whether the post will be promoted—business accounts have more restrictions and some tracks are not cleared for commercial/paid use.",
    "There is no single legal or industry numeric definition of 'fast' Wi‑Fi; required throughput depends on use case and number of simultaneous users.",
    "The term 'handcrafted' is not automatically unlawful in U.S. advertising, but under FTC truth‑in‑advertising standards any impression created must be supportable (i.e., the claim must not be misleading).",
    "Auto captions exist but are not a substitute for edited/burned captions for production-quality messaging; verify and edit for clarity."
  ],
  "claims_requiring_verification": [
    "Brew Haven actually provides 'free fast Wi‑Fi' to customer seats at peak times — requires on‑site speed tests across multiple seats/times.",
    "Brew Haven's coffee/process qualifies as 'handcrafted' as implied in the script — requires internal documentation of preparation practices or process description.",
    "Permission/license to use the chosen lo‑fi acoustic loop or other music/SFX on a business Instagram account and for paid promotion — requires the specific track and territory license review.",
    "Any numeric/percentage claims about the target audience (e.g., 'X% of 22–35-year-olds work from cafés') — requires a locally appropriate survey or dependable secondary source with matching cohort and geography.",
    "Competitor case study claims about foot traffic lift from Reels — requires seller/owner-provided measurement or third‑party case study with methodology."
  ],
  "important_corrections": [
    "Do not present a specific percentage of young professionals (22–35) who work from cafés without a local survey or a cited source that matches the cohort and geography.",
    "Do not assume in‑app music is cleared for commercial/paid promotion—business use often requires separate clearance or use of Meta Sound Collection.",
    "Avoid making an unqualified 'fast' Wi‑Fi claim without repeated, dated tests during peak customer periods and documented results."
  ],
  "creative_relevant_insights": [
    "Hook in first 1–2 seconds: show a clear scene of someone settled with laptop + coffee to immediately communicate 'workable space.'",
    "Visually show evidence of the claim: include a visible Wi‑Fi icon on a small sign or a quick screen capture of device showing network name (if allowed) plus a shot of outlets and seating to substantiate 'work nooks.'",
    "Use burned‑in captions and a clear cover frame; keep on‑screen text minimal and centered within safe area to avoid UI overlap.",
    "If you plan to boost the Reel, secure a commercial license for the music before promotion; alternatively use Meta Sound Collection to avoid licensing issues.",
    "Collect simple measurement signals to prove business impact: direction clicks from the post/ad, stamp a small in‑shop survey at point of sale ('How did you hear about us?'), or track a time‑limited offer redemptions (if permitted)."
  ],
  "research_gaps": [
    "On‑site Wi‑Fi test results (speed, latency, packet loss) at Brew Haven during peak and off‑peak times — must be provided by client/operations or tested by production team.",
    "Documented definition/process that substantiates 'handcrafted' for Brew Haven's coffee drinks (who prepares, manual steps, automation) — client must provide.",
    "Specific music track choice (title/artist/source) or confirmation that Meta Sound Collection will be used — needed to confirm licensing for business/paid promotion.",
    "Local competitor examples with measured outcomes (foot traffic or direction clicks) in the Brew Haven market (likely PDX) — client/local media agency can supply.",
    "Confirm Brew Haven's city/primary store to tailor location‑specific CTA best practices and local restrictions (brief uses '@brewhavenpdx' but production should confirm exact targeting geography)."
  ],
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "2024 State of Remote Work",
      "domain": "buffer.com",
      "date": "2024"
    },
    {
      "title": "American Time Use Survey (ATUS)",
      "domain": "bls.gov",
      "date": "annual / most recent"
    },
    {
      "title": "The Future of Jobs Report 2025",
      "domain": "weforum.org",
      "date": "2025"
    },
    {
      "title": "Reels ads guide / specifications",
      "domain": "facebook.com/business/help",
      "date": "current guidance (per Perplexity)"
    },
    {
      "title": "Instagram Help Center — Music & Copyright",
      "domain": "help.instagram.com",
      "date": "current guidance (per Perplexity)"
    },
    {
      "title": "Meta Sound Collection",
      "domain": "facebook.com/business/help",
      "date": "current guidance (per Perplexity)"
    },
    {
      "title": "Zoom — System requirements for meetings",
      "domain": "support.zoom.us",
      "date": "current guidance (per Perplexity)"
    },
    {
      "title": "Measuring Broadband America (methodology / context)",
      "domain": "fcc.gov",
      "date": "2024"
    },
    {
      "title": "Speedtest by Ookla (testing tool / guidance)",
      "domain": "speedtest.net",
      "date": "current"
    },
    {
      "title": "FTC Policy Statement on Deception / Advertising guidance",
      "domain": "ftc.gov",
      "date": "1983 (policy) / 2019–2023 supplemental guidance"
    },
    {
      "title": "Meta Ad Library",
      "domain": "facebook.com/ads/library",
      "date": "current"
    },
    {
      "title": "Meta Business Success Stories / Ad case studies",
      "domain": "facebook.com/business/success",
      "date": "current"
    }
  ],
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "Exact, current Instagram/Meta music licensing rules for business accounts in Brew Haven's territory can change frequently—verify in Ads Manager/Help Center immediately before boosting or paid promotion.",
    "Local consumer behavior for Brew Haven's specific market (PDX) and the precise prevalence of 22–35-year-olds using cafés as workspaces—requires a short local survey or first‑party data to quantify.",
    "Direct evidence linking similar Reels to measured foot‑traffic lifts: public engagement metrics exist, but conversion (visits) must be measured by the advertiser—no validated public case studies were found that tie a café Reel to foot traffic with verifiable methodology.",
    "The practical Wi‑Fi '25 Mbps down / 5 Mbps up per active user' guideline is a conservative operational recommendation derived from typical app requirements — not an industry legal standard; actual needed bandwidth depends on concurrency and app mix."
  ]
}

creative_content:
"{
  "status": "PROCEED",
  "creative_director_output": {
    "objective": "Drive foot traffic to Brew Haven by communicating it as a welcoming, productive spot for remote work (cozy seating, handcrafted coffee, and reliable Wi‑Fi).",
    "audience": "Young professionals, age 22–35, who work remotely and seek a cozy, quiet place to focus.",
    "audience_insight": "Remote young professionals value a change of scenery and gentle ambient stimulation; they choose third places that combine good coffee, comfortable work nooks, and reliable connectivity so they can be productive away from home.",
    "core_problem_or_desire": "They need a comfortable, low-friction workspace outside the home that supports focused work and small meetings without feeling like a noisy café.",
    "value_proposition": "Brew Haven is a warm, quiet café designed for productive remote work—handcrafted coffee, calm work nooks, and free fast Wi‑Fi (subject to verification).",
    "core_message": "Cozy. Quiet. Connected.",
    "creative_angle": "Warm, authentic lifestyle slice: show a peaceful morning at Brew Haven where someone settles in with a laptop and a handcrafted drink, visually demonstrating the hospitality and practical amenities that enable focused work.",
    "big_idea": "Find your focus at Brew Haven — the cozy corner that helps your work click.",
    "hook": "0–2s visual hook: a person arriving/settling with laptop + coffee in warm morning light (immediately communicates 'workable space').",
    "supporting_points": [
      "Handcrafted coffee (visual: latte art / barista shot).",
      "Quiet corners & comfortable seating (visual: medium shots of nooks and outlets).",
      "Free fast Wi‑Fi (visual: subtle Wi‑Fi icon / customer on video call or device with connection indicator).",
      "Warm, calming atmosphere that supports productivity (lighting, slow camera moves)."
    ],
    "tone": "Warm, inviting, calm, slightly aspirational — focused on comfort and productivity rather than hype.",
    "visual_direction": "15s vertical (9:16, 1080×1920) — color palette cream (#F6EFE6), espresso brown (#3B2B20), soft amber (#D69A56). Use warm, slightly desaturated grade with amber highlights. Gentle push-ins, slow pans, soft cross-dissolves; no fast cuts. Text aligned center-left in safe area; Montserrat-style sans-serif. Burned-in captions for VO. End card: cream background, espresso-brown text with CTA and @brewhavenpdx centered.",
    "story_structure": [
      {
        "0:00-0:02": "Establishing shot — warm exterior/wide interior; on-screen text 'Brew Haven' (cream on espresso-brown translucent bar). Ambient café SFX + soft strum; no VO."
      },
      {
        "0:02-0:06": "Close-up of barista pulling espresso / latte art; gentle camera push-in. VO: 'Need a cozy spot to get work done?' Subtle on-screen text."
      },
      {
        "0:06-0:10": "Medium shots of remote-worker scenes (typing, headphones in nook, smiling with coffee). On-screen icons: small Wi‑Fi symbol 'Free fast Wi‑Fi', tiny coffee icon 'Handcrafted'. VO: 'Handcrafted coffee, quiet corners, and free fast Wi‑Fi.'"
      },
      {
        "0:10-0:13": "Over-the-shoulder laptop + notebook shot; soft time-lapse sunlight. VO: 'Stay focused. Stay inspired.'"
      },
      {
        "0:13-0:15": "End card: cream background with espresso-brown text 'Visit Brew Haven today' and '@brewhavenpdx' centered. VO CTA."
      }
    ],
    "cta": "Visit Brew Haven today. (Display @brewhavenpdx on final frame)",
    "creative_concepts": [
      {
        "name": "Primary Draft (as briefed)",
        "description": "15s vertical Reel following the provided script and shot plan with AI-generated visuals, warm female VO, lo‑fi acoustic loop from Meta Sound Collection (recommended). Burned-in captions and safe-area text placement."
      },
      {
        "name": "Compliance-Safe Variant",
        "description": "Same edit but soften or qualify any potentially factual impression: replace 'Handcrafted' icon text with 'Freshly made by our baristas' or 'Pulled to order' if client cannot substantiate 'handcrafted'. Use Meta Sound Collection track to avoid licensing risk for paid promotion."
      },
      {
        "name": "Evidence-Forward Variant (optional paid/boosted)",
        "description": "If client supplies on-site assets or verification (Wi‑Fi test logs, barista process photos), swap AI visuals for real assets or add a quick frame showing Wi‑Fi speed test or barista at work to strengthen verifiability before paid promotion."
      }
    ],
    "claims_and_evidence": [
      {
        "claim": "Free fast Wi‑Fi",
        "evidence_required": "On-site speed tests (recorded Speedtest results) across multiple seats and peak/off-peak times with dates/times/locations. If tests vary, use a qualified phrasing (e.g., 'suitable for browsing & video calls')."
      },
      {
        "claim": "Handcrafted coffee",
        "evidence_required": "Client documentation of preparation practices (which steps are manual, who prepares drinks). If unavailable, soften language to avoid implying a specific, unverifiable process."
      },
      {
        "claim": "Music usage",
        "evidence_required": "License or confirmation that chosen track is cleared for business accounts and paid promotion in Brew Haven's territory. Recommendation: use Meta Sound Collection track for initial produce/boost-safe version."
      }
    ],
    "risks_and_constraints": [
      "Do not state additional factual claims beyond script; avoid numeric audience claims without client-supplied data.",
      "Music licensing: business account and paid promotion restrictions — verify license before boosting.",
      "Wi‑Fi performance claim must be substantiated if client requires unqualified 'fast' — otherwise qualify the language.",
      "'Handcrafted' may create factual expectations under FTC guidance — verify or soften.",
      "AI-generated visuals: they are illustrative, not documentary; avoid implying footage is of Brew Haven staff/customers if client lacks permission or real assets.",
      "Keep critical text inside safe zone to avoid Reels UI overlap; burned-in captions required for sound-off viewers."
    ],
    "downstream_instructions": "Production & pre-publish checklist:\n1) Produce 9:16 master (1080×1920) using AI-generated assets per brief; ensure all on-screen text is within safe margins and high-contrast. Choose clear cover frame. 2) Use Meta Sound Collection track for first draft to avoid licensing risk; if client prefers a specific third-party track, obtain written commercial + paid-promotion license before finalizing/boosting. 3) Burn edited captions matching VO; QA for timing/legibility. 4) Confirm with client whether 'handcrafted' is supportable; if not, use alternate phrasing ('pulled to order' / 'freshly made'). 5) Request or perform Wi‑Fi speed tests if client insists on unqualified 'fast' claim; otherwise flag the claim internally and consider qualified phrasing. 6) Preview in Instagram/Ads Manager to confirm UI-safe composition and test thumbnails. 7) For measurement, prepare tracking: enable direction-click tracking on boosted posts, and/or set an optional in-store 'How did you hear about us?' at POS. 8) Keep dated records for any substantiating evidence (Wi‑Fi tests, barista process docs, music license) to support claims if needed.\n\nValidation note: Anthropic validation tool was invoked and returned a PROCEED recommendation with the mitigations above; their assessment has been incorporated into these downstream instructions and risk mitigations."
  }
}"
